WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.240
Was there ever a post office in Mossville?

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:03.440
Yeah.

3
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.160
Not in my time, but there was a post office there.

4
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.880
Do you know where it was?

5
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.340
It was over here by this railroad track.

6
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.160
On the west side of the railroad tracks, so I'm told.

7
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.760
James Moss was the postmaster.

8
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.940
We called him Jim, Jim Moss.

9
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.540
You knew him?

10
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.480
Oh yeah, I knew him.

11
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.860
I don't know if he knows me, was an old man then.

12
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.600
But yes, I knew him.

13
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.380
James Moss.

14
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.140
Where did he live?

15
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:34.840
He lived back up here on the other side of Prater Road.

16
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.740
There's a Baptist church up there on the right side of the road.

17
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.460
He lived on the south side of the road there.

18
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:48.445
All that property around here now as you go from the gully near the south side of the road, that was his.

19
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:50.320
Jim Moss.

20
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.500
What did your mom tell you about the post office?

21
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.600
Oh, she said it just went down.

22
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:04.460
Just did nothing about it after James Moss died.

23
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.540
They didn't have another postmaster general.

24
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:16.260
And my conclusion is what she was saying is that they didn’t have nobody have sense enough to come down here and run the post office and distribute the mail and pick it up.

25
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.200
I don't believe you need to be educated to do that.

26
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:27.120
That's rules and things you need to know according to the postal rules, but I believe anybody can dispatch a mail truck.

27
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.260
It's so easy because it's Mossville.

28
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.140
Because we know everybody in Mossville.

29
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.998
You ain't even got to study who lives where.

30
00:01:33.998 --> 00:01:34.564
"Who this here?

31
00:01:34.564 --> 00:01:35.320
What's his address?"

32
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.820
You know everybody in Mossville.

33
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:46.480
Should be just that easy, but that's not what it is.
